+# BLUE CURRENT V51.60.0 — PILOT EXECUTION & OBSERVATION CONTROL
+
+V51.56–V51.60 adds the human-controlled execution/observation layer that sits after launch authorization.
+
+## Ordered first-live milestones
+
+1. PILOT_START
+2. FIRST_OPERATOR_LOGIN
+3. FIRST_RESERVATION_WORKFLOW
+4. FIRST_SEATING_WORKFLOW
+5. FIRST_SERVICE_FLOW
+6. FIRST_KITCHEN_WORKFLOW
+7. SUPPORT_BRIDGE_ACTIVE
+
+Milestones must be confirmed in order.
+
+Every milestone requires human evidence.
+
+Blue Current records the observation; it does not perform the underlying restaurant action.
+
+## Explicit pilot start
+
+A pilot execution session cannot begin until V51.55 has a:
+
+`PILOT_LAUNCH_AUTHORIZED`
+
+record.
+
+Starting the V51.60 session requires human start evidence.
+
+The start record explicitly states:
+
+- runtimeStartedByService: false
+- guestActionPerformed: false
+- operationalMutationPerformed: false
+
+## Health observation
+
+Live health observations cover:
+
+- API health
+- authentication health
+- reservation workflow health
+- floor workflow health
+- kitchen workflow health
+- support bridge health
+
+Severity:
+
+- none
+- low
+- medium
+- high
+- critical
+
+High/critical observations require an incident description.
+
+## Human operating decision
+
+The launch owner/executive can record:
+
+- CONTINUE
+- HOLD
+- ROLLBACK
+
+CONTINUE normally requires:
+
+- all seven first-live milestones
+- a fully healthy latest observation
+- zero high/critical incident observations
+
+An executive can still record CONTINUE with open criteria only with a documented reason.
+
+HOLD and ROLLBACK always require a human reason.
+
+## Important separation
+
+A ROLLBACK decision is a human recommendation/decision record.
+
+It does not execute rollback.
+
+V51.60 does not:
+
+- start the runtime
+- make the first reservation
+- seat a guest
+- advance service flow
+- change kitchen state
+- contact guests
+- automatically mitigate incidents
+- automatically roll back production
+
+## Current authenticated Chefs runtime
+
+Current untouched authoritative state:
+
+`pilot-execution-awaiting-start`
+
+All five locations currently show:
+
+- execution ready: false
+- milestones: 0/7
+- high/critical incidents: 0
+
+This is expected because V51.55 launch authorization has not yet been written to the authoritative database.
+
+## Safety policy
+
+- launch authorization required
+- explicit human start record required
+- milestone evidence required
+- live health observation required
+- human CONTINUE/HOLD/ROLLBACK decision required
+- decisions do not execute rollback
+- no autonomous pilot execution
+- no automatic guest actions
+- no automatic operational mutation
+- autonomous production changes false
+
+## Validation
+
+- V51.60 focused execution lifecycle PASS
+- explicit pilot-start record PASS
+- first operator login PASS
+- first reservation workflow PASS
+- first seating workflow PASS
+- first service-flow workflow PASS
+- first kitchen workflow PASS
+- support bridge status PASS
+- launch incident logging PASS
+- live health observation PASS
+- CONTINUE/HOLD/ROLLBACK decision flow PASS
+- milestone-order enforcement PASS
+- critical-incident evidence guard PASS
+- no automatic rollback PASS
+- V51.55 regression PASS
+- authenticated execution endpoint PASS
+- authoritative database unchanged
+- undefined module exports: 0
+- duplicate HTML IDs: 0
+- npm run check PASS
+- 953 JavaScript files
+- 794 client scripts
+- 5,945 unique HTML IDs
+
+## Next
+
+V51.61–V51.65 — Pilot Stabilization & Exit Criteria
+
+- repeated live-health observations
+- incident trend
+- operator confidence
+- workflow stability
+- guest-impact review
+- support load
+- data-integrity recheck
+- executive KPI trust recheck
+- stabilization window
+- explicit human STABLE / EXTEND / ROLLBACK decision
+- pilot-exit evidence
